    EditorialLessonRecord("Class 11–12|Atomic Structure: Senior Secondary|Atomic number and mass number",
        "explicit topic alias",
        "Atomic number is the number of protons in an atom's nucleus.\n\nMass number is the total number of protons and neutrons in one atom's nucleus.",
        "It is written Z and uniquely identifies an element. Changing the number of electrons makes an ion, but changing the proton count makes a different element.\n\nIt is a whole number written A. Electrons contribute so little mass that they are not counted in the mass number.",
